+# CALL OF DUTY: BLACK OPS III v01.06 and v01.07, BLES02166 -- ours. Freezes a few seconds after the profile
+# loads: main_thread waits for a job type's counters to reach zero and they never do.
+#
+# The game runs its streaming jobs on the SPUs through its own job manager. Each job type keeps a
+# queued and a running count, and a job whose dependencies are busy goes back on the queue. In this
+# version staticsurfaces waits while dynamicmodels is queued or running, and dynamicmodels waits
+# while staticsurfaces is queued or running. Both are queued each frame, 1.8 ms apart. If
+# staticsurfaces has not started by the time dynamicmodels is queued, each sees the other pending
+# and both requeue forever (traced on the macOS test build: millions of requeues, no further
+# progress). The disc release, 01.00, has only the second wait, so the race came in with an update;
+# it shows up here because an SPU can take a few milliseconds to pick a job up.
+#
+# The patch makes staticsurfaces wait only while dynamicmodels is running. Its queued-count helper
+# (LS 0x6cc8 in the job image, at 0xc0d480 in 01.06 and 0xc09c80 in 01.07, the same bytes in both)
+# reads the running count instead, and the dynamicmodels check
+# calls it. The two jobs still never run together: each raises its own running count before it
+# checks the other. Its other use, the queued count of treenodes, is also covered by the busy check
+# of treenodes that follows. Offsets are guest addresses in the executable's data.
